WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:06.075
Runbook R02 is Phase 0: count everything
first, decide what survives second.

2
00:00:06.075 --> 00:00:09.556
Discovery is read-only; the
consolidation it leads to

3
00:00:09.556 --> 00:00:13.038
is review-required and
belongs to the migration plan.

4
00:00:13.038 --> 00:00:15.874
The inventory starts from
the program's scripts.

5
00:00:15.874 --> 00:00:19.324
The D1.8 audit script, run
in discovery-only form,

6
00:00:19.324 --> 00:00:25.249
finds instances from their SQL Server SPNs
and an explicit target list and reads

7
00:00:25.249 --> 00:00:28.964
each host's services over
CIM; without a connection,

8
00:00:28.964 --> 00:00:32.413
version and authentication
mode read Unknown.

9
00:00:32.413 --> 00:00:39.246
The D1.5 SPN inventory gives the domain's
SPN trail, with duplicates and orphans:

10
00:00:39.246 --> 00:00:44.713
SPNs on disabled objects, or on
objects with no logon in 180 days.

11
00:00:44.713 --> 00:00:46.906
Those scripts miss what has no SPN,

12
00:00:46.906 --> 00:00:51.608
like an Express instance an installer
dropped on an application server,

13
00:00:51.608 --> 00:00:55.683
so cast wider with Find-DbaInstance,
a forest-wide SetSPN query,

14
00:00:55.683 --> 00:00:58.974
and Azure Migrate or the
Arc migration assessment.

15
00:00:58.974 --> 00:01:02.825
Then the program's estate-inventory
function fuses the sources.

16
00:01:02.825 --> 00:01:08.287
It keys every instance on host and
instance name, so duplicates collapse,

17
00:01:08.287 --> 00:01:14.387
records which instruments found each one,
and applies a first pass on two signals:

18
00:01:14.387 --> 00:01:17.756
last access at or above
400 days means retire,

19
00:01:17.756 --> 00:01:22.763
a pre-2022 engine means consolidate,
and 2022 or later means retain.

20
00:01:22.763 --> 00:01:27.788
Anything without enough signal lands
in review, never silently in retain.

21
00:01:27.788 --> 00:01:30.349
The lenses come next, with one caution.

22
00:01:30.349 --> 00:01:34.017
The index-usage DMV resets
whenever the engine starts,

23
00:01:34.017 --> 00:01:38.825
so it can't prove 400 days of disuse
unless the instance has run that long.

24
00:01:38.825 --> 00:01:43.771
Read the start time beside it, and take
long-horizon evidence from login auditing,

25
00:01:43.771 --> 00:01:46.650
backup history and the
application portfolio.

26
00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:50.947
For dependencies, read
sys.servers and the linked logins,

27
00:01:50.947 --> 00:01:54.512
plus the Agent, replication
and SSIS footprint.

28
00:01:54.512 --> 00:01:59.988
Finally the architects confirm or override
each verdict, with the reason recorded.

29
00:01:59.988 --> 00:02:02.291
The evidence is the sealed inventory,

30
00:02:02.291 --> 00:02:05.562
with its classification
counts and its denominator.

31
00:02:05.562 --> 00:02:08.655
And schedule network sweeps
with security operations,

32
00:02:08.655 --> 00:02:11.140
because intrusion detection can flag them.
